{#
  DIRECTION CONTRACT
  THESIS: The resources index reads as the platform's own library, not a
  bolted-on blog — homepage-v2's navy/green/glass system carries a
  content-browsing task instead of a marketing narrative.
  OWN-WORLD: #F8FAFC/white ground, #76B900 the one accent (badges, active
  filter states, CTA), navy-950 dark cards for the featured banner and CTA,
  mono uppercase eyebrows/labels, rounded-2xl glass-tinted cards
  (border-white/60, gradient sky-100/60 via sky-50/25 to white/50,
  backdrop-blur-sm, shadow-subtle), Inter at homepage-v2 weights.
  STORY: visitor scans the featured story, sees the standout report, then
  filters/browses the full library and converts on a CTA that matches the
  rest of the site.
  FIRST VIEWPORT: left-aligned "Resources" H1 over a featured story (image +
  meta + title) with a "More Resources" list beside it — same structural
  split as before, homepage-v2's card and type vocabulary applied.
  FORM: extend the established homepage-v2/what-is-gaas world onto this
  index — content, data bindings, and filter logic inherited unchanged, no
  new visual system invented.
#}

{% include "partials/navbar-v2.njk" %}

<script>
  document.documentElement.classList.add('js-reveal-hidden');
</script>
